From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: no_trace <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 10:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ghosthook: rewind EL0 single-step after a consumed trace event

The bounded SS core consumes HWSS before Linux's stock single_step_handler.
The stock handler normally calls user_rewind_single_step(), which converts
the debug state back to active-not-pending by restoring SPSR.SS for the next
EL0 return.  The custom consume path omitted that operation: hardware kept
raising the same pending event and every ring record contained the same PC.

Rewind only while this session remains active.  At the configured final hit
the existing disable path wins, preserving the bounded self-terminating
contract and foreign ptrace/perf single-step ownership rules.

---
 arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
index 39f7ce9..0000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
@@ -138,10 +138,13 @@ static bool gh_ss_trace_debug_event(unsigned long addr_if_watchpoint,
 	gh_ss_trace_record_locked(regs);
 	gh_ss_trace.hits++;
 	if (gh_ss_trace.hits >= gh_ss_trace.limit) {
 		/* The bounded session owns this SS request and may clear it. */
 		user_disable_single_step(current);
 		gh_ss_trace.ss_owned = false;
 		gh_ss_trace.active = false;
+	} else {
+		/* We consumed HWSS before stock single_step_handler's rewind. */
+		user_rewind_single_step(current);
 	}
 	consumed = true;
 out:
 	raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&gh_ss_trace_lock, flags);
 	return consumed;
-- 
